{
  "rationale": "The plant automata model the robot's motion commands and perception outcomes. The specification automata enforce safe, conservative obstacle avoidance and steady exploration, alternating between random_walk and short forward pulses, with dedicated recovery states for obstacles. Recovery uses minimal turns and only escalates to full_rotate if repeatedly blocked. The design ensures no forward or random_walk in obstacle states, and always returns to exploration as soon as the path is clear.",
  "strategy": [
    "Separate plant automata for motion and perception to reflect modular robot subsystems.",
    "Specification automata bind perception outcomes to safe, progress-oriented actions, enforcing conservative recovery and rapid return to exploration."
  ],
